><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://vigeoretreats.com/retreat/the-wholehearted-woman-retreat/&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Learn More about this Retreat&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:&quot;button-wrapper&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary button-wrapper\" href=\"https://vigeoretreats.com/retreat/the-wholehearted-woman-retreat/\"><span>Learn More about this Retreat</span></a></p><div><hr></div><h3>New to Retreats with Erin? </h3><p>Here’s what to expect.</p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://mindfulmoments.sg/retreats/what-to-expect&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Retreat Guide&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://mindfulmoments.sg/retreats/what-to-expect\"><span>Retreat Guide</span></a></p><p></p>",
  "body_text": "Four sessions into our Dhammapada-inspired series, the text offers us a few metaphors:\n\nThrough effort, vigilance, \nRestraint, and self-control, \nThe wise person can become an island \nNo flood will overwhelm.\n\n(verse 25, trans. Gil Fronsdal)\n\nWe do not go looking for the island. We become it.\n\nThe floods in our life are ordinary enough. They are other people’s opinions of your work, a conflict you did not ask for, the plain uncertainty of being alive. \n\nThey come and go as they wish, and they will not stop coming because you have started practicing.\n\nThe text then turns from water to wind: \n\nA solid mass of rock is not moved by the wind (verse 81).\n\nIn the teachings there are eight worldly winds - gain and loss, pleasure and pain, praise and blame, fame and disrepute. The pleasant four blow just as hard as the others, only because we hold them tightly and they leave anyway.\n\nNow don’t be mistaken — being a rock is not being cold, or unresponsive, or hidden away. The rock sits bravely out in the open. It meets the wind, and it stays.\n\nOneself, indeed, is one’s own protector. What other protector could there be? (verse 160)\n\nThis verse sits in a chapter called Oneself, which is not about self-importance. It is about ownership. \n\nWe can have teachers we trust and wise friends we lean on, but they guide us from outside. \n\nTaking ownership of our own mind means staying with ourselves in difficulty rather than abandoning ourselves there, and being willing to say: I am worth this effort.\n\n---\n\nAt Take A Pause Live on Insight Timer over 15-16 August 2026, we cultivated our inner refuge through staying with the body in the midst of “floods” and “winds”. We shared a reading from Erin’s book, Take A Pause: Waking Up to a Life of Clarity. \n\nMeditation Practice\n\nTap Play to Practice Together:\n\nThis post is free for some time, and then archived for paid subscribers to support a sustainable, long-term sharing of mindful content. To support Erin’s work, upgrade to receive lifetime access to the full archive and ongoing updates.\n\nShare\n\n---\n\nThe Wholehearted Woman Retreat\n\n1–5 October 2026 · Siem Reap, Cambodia\n\nwith Erin Lee\n\n*Early bird rate available \n\nLearn More about this Retreat\n\n---\n\nNew to Retreats with Erin? \n\nHere’s what to expect.\n\nRetreat Guide",
